course: dictionary
lesson: 4238
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. «Even top chess players, called grandmasters, lose games; going over a lost game is one of the best ways to improve.» The clues top chess players show that grandmasters means chess players of the highest standard.
explain: In chess, grandmaster is a real title. It is the highest title a player can win, given by the World Chess Federation (FIDE) to the very best players. It is not just a nickname for a clever player.
explain: Outside chess, a grandmaster can be a great expert, as in «a grandmaster of magic», or the head of some clubs, knightly orders or martial arts schools. To choose the right meaning, look at the clues around the word and ask: what is this sentence about?
fact: Grandmaster is a noun. Its plural is grandmasters.
fact: In chess, a grandmaster is the highest title a player can win, given by FIDE.
fact: GM is the short form of grandmaster, often used after a chess player's name.
fact: Some players become grandmasters as teenagers.
fact: Magnus Carlsen is a famous chess grandmaster.
exercise: In «Even top chess players, called grandmasters, lose games», what does grandmasters mean? | Teachers who write chess books | Anyone who has just learned the rules | People who play only for fun | *The very best chess players, who hold the highest title
exercise: «He is a grandmaster of magic.» What does grandmaster suggest here? | A card that is worth a lot | A magician's helper | *A great expert at magic | A beginner who has just started
exercise: Which short form is often used for a chess grandmaster? | GP | MG | *GM | GS
test: Which organisation gives the grandmaster title in chess? | FIFA | UNESCO | NASA | *FIDE
test: In a sentence about a martial arts school, what might Grandmaster mean? | *The head of the school | A beginner with a white belt | A kind of training shoe | A referee's whistle
exam: Which clue in «Even top chess players, called grandmasters, lose games» tells you the meaning? | The comma | The word even | *The words top chess players | The word called
